# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in only what you need.
# Nothing here is required — the app runs without any of it, and each variable
# just enables an optional capability.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alignment sidecar  (recommended — this is what times uploaded audio)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Python service in ./asr-service. See asr-service/README.md to set it up.
# No API key, no per-request cost, and audio never leaves your machine.
# ASR_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Which matcher /api/audio/match uses when the client doesn't pick one:
#
#   align  - RECOMMENDED ("Local" in the studio). Force-aligns known Quran text
#            against the audio, so a word cannot be dropped, garbled, or put in
#            the wrong surah. Needs the sidecar.
#   gemini - "Online" in the studio. Cloud only, zero setup. Timing is an
#            estimate, not a measurement.
#
# See docs/ALIGNMENT.md for the comparison.
# AUDIO_MATCH_PROVIDER=align

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quran Foundation API  (needed only for The Clear Quran)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The studio reads Quran text and translations from api.quran.com, which is
# open, keyless, and publishes 126 translations. What that list does NOT
# include is The Clear Quran (Dr. Mustafa Khattab, resource 131): quran.com's
# own site serves it from the Quran Foundation API instead, and asking the open
# API for 131 returns HTTP 200 with the translation silently missing.
#
# Request a free client at https://api-docs.quran.foundation and set both
# halves. With them set, every Quran fetch goes through that API, 131 becomes
# available in the picker, and it becomes the default translation.
#
# Read https://api-docs.quran.foundation/legal/developer-terms/ first. Two
# clauses matter for a video studio: content may not be cached or stored beyond
# 7 days (saved projects and drafts keep verse text indefinitely), and the
# Quran text may not be modified (the inspector lets you edit it). Ask
# [email protected] if you intend to publish exported videos.
# QURAN_FOUNDATION_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
# QURAN_FOUNDATION_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret

# `prelive` uses the Foundation's sandbox, which issues separate credentials.
# QURAN_FOUNDATION_ENV=live

# Which translation a caption's own text is. Defaults to 20 (Saheeh
# International) on the open API and 131 (The Clear Quran) once Foundation
# credentials are set. Set both of these together if you want something else --
# the server reads the first, the browser reads the second, and they are meant
# to agree.
# QURAN_TRANSLATION_ID=131
# NEXT_PUBLIC_QURAN_TRANSLATION_ID=131

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini  (needed only for the `gemini` matcher)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — the free tier is enough
# to try it. GOOGLE_API_KEY works as an alternative name.
# Inline audio is limited to roughly 18 MB (about 15-20 minutes of MP3).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Must be a current model that accepts audio input. Model IDs are retired
# regularly — gemini-2.0-flash and gemini-2.5-flash are already gone and return
# HTTP 404. Check https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models before setting.
# (chirp_3 is a Speech-to-Text model, not a Gemini model, and will not work.)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# Ceiling on a single Gemini request, in milliseconds.
# GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS=180000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pexels  (optional — only for pasting Pexels *page* links as backgrounds)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free key at https://www.pexels.com/api/. With it, the background field accepts
# a page link copied straight from the address bar
# (https://www.pexels.com/video/...-34918472/) and resolves it to the video file.
# Without it, use the download menu on Pexels, copy the file link, and paste
# that instead — everything else works the same.
# PEXELS_API_KEY=your_pexels_api_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sharing this beyond your own machine  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this and the whole studio requires the token; leave it unset and there is
# no authentication at all, which is fine on localhost and nowhere else.
#
# Without it, anyone who can reach the app can list and delete every saved
# project, spend your Gemini key, and spend your Pexels quota. With it, open
# the studio once as http://host:3000/?token=<the token> — that is exchanged
# for an HttpOnly cookie and stripped from the URL. Scripts can send
# `Authorization: Bearer <the token>` instead. /api/health stays open so an
# uptime check does not need the secret.
#
# This is a shared secret, not a login: it says the caller is you, not which
# user they are. Multi-user hosting needs real accounts. Use a long random
# value — `openssl rand -hex 32` — and serve over HTTPS.
# STUDIO_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this, saved projects and exports live in memory and are lost when the
# server restarts.
#
# IMPORTANT: leave this commented out unless you have a database running. The
# API checks whether the variable is SET, not whether it connects, so a
# placeholder value skips the in-memory fallback and makes every save return
# HTTP 500. See the "Database (optional)" section of README.md for setup.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://quranclipper:quranclipper@127.0.0.1:5432/quranclipper
